A||N||4||Jeff Blowers||Ignition Failure||||1||
Z||000000||Jeff Blowers||10-14-2001||10:13 AM||||My 2.8 has been hard starting and running rough below 2K RPM.  I have been chasing ignition problems since installing an Accel coil.  Changed ignition module recently, and this weekend replaced the distributor pick up coil.  Now the car will not even start.  I can't seem to find a description of the an external condensor (I think) mounted on the block near the distributor?  Would like to replace it also.  Any thoughts on this, or anything else?||||reg||1
Z||000001||daved||10-14-2001||10:23 AM||||That external "condensor" is actually a filter for the tachometer, and often fails, causing all kinds of ignition gremlins.  Start by disconnecting it & post your findings to help us narrow it down.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jeff Blowers||10-14-2001||10:56 AM||||I disconnected the filter (unplugged the connector).  No change.  I am scratching my head on this one.  This no start problem happened after replacing the distributor pick up coil yesterday. This morning I even put the old one back in just to make sure the new part was not bad out of the box.  I was careful both time to make sure the rotor pointed the same way so as to not screw up timing.  I am really missing something here.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-14-2001||11:01 AM||||since you didnt have the problem before changing the PU coil, Id have to guess your main problem is somewhere there. Bad connector, bad cap, hooked up backward, shorted and fried new module? Your ECM ok?||||reg||1
Z||000004||daved||10-15-2001||11:10 PM||||Jeff, pull an ignition wire and put in an old plug. Ground the plug threads to the block, and crank.  Do you get a series of nice sparks?  If yes, then timing is probably out. Use a timing light to get it close, then time properly with the ECM in diagnostic mode when you get it going. <P>If not, then you hooked up something wrong. Good luck!||||reg||1
